From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Olivet <jordanolivet@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 01:07:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: deadlock from re-entrant getChunk during chunk loading
 (+ sync-load stall watchdog)

A C2ME chunk-loading worker (e.g. a FlowSched WorkerThread running a chunk's light
step) could re-enter getChunk(..., create=true) for a not-yet-FULL chunk via a mod's
getBlockEntity -- e.g. treechop's ChoppedLogBlock.getShape during StarLight/ScalableLux
edge checks -- and block forever, because the awaited status can only be reached once
that very task finishes (often for the same chunk: its object is already a full
WorldChunk while its scheduler status is still initialize_light). A server thread
blocked in a synchronous getChunkBlocking for that chunk then deadlocks too. Triggered
in production by Mekanism force-chunk reinstatement, FTB Chunks login force-load, and
the butcher MCreator mod reading unloaded chunks under the Async mod.

Fix (re-entrancy barrier): in shortcutGetChunk, a chunk-loading thread (a FlowSched
WorkerThread, or any thread currently running a ChunkTaskWork) returns the
best-available chunk (getLatest) instead of blocking on a re-entrant getChunk.

Also adds, behind -Dc2me.syncLoadStallThresholdMs (default 8000ms, 0 disables), a
SyncLoadStallWatchdog that, when a main-thread getChunkBlocking stalls, logs the stuck
chunk holder's scheduler state (status/target/per-status futures/unsatisfied deps) plus
a filtered thread dump of the C2ME worker/scheduler/storage threads -- the exact
artifacts needed to diagnose such stalls on a headless JRE. A /c2me synctest debug
command forces synchronous far-chunk loads for testing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

